{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition","id":348065,"title":"Changes between 1st and 2nd edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-22T23:52:58-08:00","id":348065,"title":"Changes between 1st and 2nd edition","content":"Probably been asked before but what will the major changes be between the the different edition of the nWoD core books Vamp,Werewolf etc and will the 1st edition books be able to be used with the 2nd edition core book rules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/500-rindel","name":"Rindel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T01:10:41-08:00","id":348114,"title":"","content":"Second edition vampire is already out its called blood and smoke. <br /> <br /> They use the God machine chronicles update as a baseline and have added some things in. There are new antagonists and tweaks to the backstory. <br /> <br /> As far as vamp goes they have made then hardier and tweaked the powers to make them a bit more terrifying","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3837-slimjimjohnson","name":"Slimjimjohnson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T01:55:43-08:00","id":348130,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/114078/World-of-Darkness-GodMachine-Rules-Update?term=god+machine\" target=\"_blank\">Here is a link</a> to the free PDF of the changes to the blue book rules. The basics are the same, but a lot of subsystems have had some overhauling, most of all the experience system. First edition material is still very much usable in second edition games, but some of it will need a little conversion work if it interfaces with any of the affected subsystems.<br /> <br /> Vampire is the only line that the second edition core book has come out for so far. All of the Disciplines have been rewritten, including both Blood Sorcery Disciplines and the Coils. They all have a lot more oomph now. Clan weaknesses have been redone as well, and now get worse as you lose Humanity.<br /> <br /> Humanity has been slightly reworked so that it actually measures how human (or inhuman) a character is instead of how well they keep to a moral code. You suffer Breaking Points for doing inhuman things like surviving something that would kill a mortal, or going months without human contact, as well as for heinous acts like murder. However, you can protect your Humanity somewhat by maintaining a relationship with one or more Touchstones - someone (or more rarely, something) that reminds you of what it means to be human. You can also take Banes - additional weaknesses mined from vampire folklore, to make a particular act not count as a Breaking Point any more, but you can only do it a limited number of times, and it makes other Breaking Points hit a bit harder.<br /> <br /> Sunlight damage is variable now, with your Humanity determining how much damage you take and your Blood Potency determining how often you take it. Now high Humanity neonates can survive brief periods in the sun as long as they take the proper precautions while jaded elders go *poof* almost instantly.<br /> <br /> Blood Potency limits on Vitae Per Turn advance much faster now, though being restricted to Kindred blood only happens at BP6 now instead of 7. However, you can get around feeding restrictions somewhat by spending enough Willpower. All vampires have a certain degree of heightened senses now as part of the base template, basically they can see in the dark and smell blood, hear heartbeats, etc. from a long distance, which increases with Blood Potency. You also add your Blood Potency to all physical dice pools while you're Frenzying.<br /> <br /> Frenzy is no longer split into anger/hunger/fear, instead every time you Frenzy, you determine with the Storyteller what the goal of that Frenzy is, which can be &quot;kill&quot;, &quot;feed&quot;, or &quot;get away&quot; but can also be something else if appropriate. Predator's Taint has been replaced with Predatory Aura, which is conceptually similar, but instead of forcing a contested roll every time two vampires meet for the first time, you just sort of passively recognize other vampires for what they are, Unseen Sense style, and you can actively challenge another vampire with your Predatory Aura if you chose to.<br /> <br /> I'm probably missing a few things, but that's the gist of the mechanical changes. The fluff has been reworked a bit as well, to give Requiem a bit more of its own identity, independent of Masquerade. Nothing drastic, but for example there's no talk of Golconda in the new core book, and it's made much more clear that Vampires probably don't all share a single common ancestor and even the five Clans, which share more in common than most other types of vampires, probably come from different origins.<br /> <br /> You can expect the other lines to have similar changes, and can read more about them on the open development blogs here on the Onyx Path website.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 12-23-2014, 05:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T06:06:41-08:00","id":348215,"title":"","content":"As for using first edition material with second edition books, there will be some on-the-fly translation needed, but significantly less than you'd think. Since the structure of rolling the dice, counting successes, failure/success/exceptional success, most traits, etc. are intact, a lot of mechanics can be used as is, with a lot more having fairly straightforward tweaks (for instance, the rule of thumb for converting 1e weapon bonuses is to reduce the bonus by one and then apply it the 2e style of adding damage instead of dice; the rough conversion for experience costs is to divide raw numbers by five or take the cost of the third dot in a progressive dot rating and divide that by five). There are a handful of mechanical corners, like powers that interact with systems that were removed or significantly altered (Morality, specific Virtues or Vices) or with game events that did not previously have a comprehensive system (Social Maneuvering). These are not too common, though.<br /> <br /> First edition setting material is easily compatible. Setting hasn't changed much, and where it has, it's mostly changed to try to better reflect the tone that was already developing across first edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T21:32:57-08:00","id":348785,"title":"","content":"I believe people may be underestimating just quite how different things are in between the editions.<br /> They aren't wrong to say that things are mostly the same mechanic wise and that only a few subsytems are different.<br /> <br /> However, the differences, to the subsystems and the change to the lore things interact in such a way as to pain a very different picture from what was painted in 1st edition.<br /> <br /> For exemple torpor is handled differently. While it is still based on a combinaition of blood potency and humanity it does tend to be quite shorter on the lower end of the scale.<br /> Also the fog of ages is now the exception rather than the rule. And there are many many ways for a vampire with sufficient aount of power (often political) to get around feeding restriction.<br /> <br /> All these factors contribute to fundamentaly change the nature of the setting. Clueless elder that can be manipulated after spending centuries if not millenia in topro aren't really a thing anymore. More often than not an elder will be able to avoid torpro more easily, stay in it for shorter length of time and still know exactly what was what when he wakes.<br /> <br /> This in turn affect kindred view of history. History is no longer this unknowable thing that can't be relied upon. Now it's a thing that should be doubted a little but since not everyone suffer from the fog of ages it can be argued that at least in the broad strokes history as the vampires knows it may be correct. There is a seed of doubt, but that's just that a seed.<br /> <br /> The removal of predator taint and replacement with the predatory aura also alter kindred society. As a result it is much less xenophobic and closed up than it was. No longer are new kindred a dangerous source of potential frenzy for other, nor are kindred easily able to tell who is older and stronger between them. Now vampire can meet new vampires easily and whitout such risks and any use of the aura is seen as a blatant agression and not easily forgiven for it is a voluntary thing.<br /> <br /> A few disciplines have changed but the one that comes to mind as having the most potential to have changed kindred society is auspex. Auspex used to be super senses wih a dose of postcognition, telepathy and astral travel (in the common and not mage sense of the term) thrown in. Now the low level of auspex are far more focused on ferreting out direct answer to questions.<br /> Before mekhet where an annoyance because you could never be quite sure of what they knew, now a mekhet can potentialy learn anything about anyone no matter what precautions are put in place.<br /> This has staggering implication for other vampire attitudes toward Mekhets, implications that have been quietly ignored and perhaps not even realised. But in my sense if you lived in a society based heavily on secrets, backstabbing and paranoia and someone showed up with the ability to tell all your secrets at a glance, not just read your mood but outright finding out factual information about you, something that was limited to whether or not you were a diablerist before but now apply to everything, You would not suffer their presence gladly. The implication is, at least to me, that mekhet should be treated like pariahs even worse than nosferatus at best and outright killed on sight at worst.<br /> <br /> Clan weaknesses have changed, making the way everyone belonging to each clan act differently from what was happening in 1st edition, somtime drasticly so.<br /> Gangrel used to be...well...somewhat dumb. Now they just have a harder time resisting frenzy. They shouldn't be seen as dumb but potentialy very dangerous, not entirely out of control, they can guide their frenzy just as well as anyone else but they will frenzy more often.<br /> <br /> Daeva were big vice indulgers, turning hedonistic out of necessity, now they they get a pseudo blood bond if they feed more than once from the same person, that makes them either supremely promscuous or supremely careful.<br /> <br /> Ventrue were prone to insanity, now they just have slightly more trouble with touchstones (it seems to be the conscencus that their clan weakness is a joke)<br /> <br /> Nosferatu however have if far easier now. Sure people are still unsettled but their curse only applies to relating to people, a nos can just as easily seduce someone else as anyone, just don't ask for them to make a good shoulder to cry on if you are human.<br /> <br /> Mekhet were suffering from worse banes than other, they still do, but they are also less able to get a thick skin, so to speak, when it comes to what prompt vampire to realise they aren't human.<br /> <br /> There are many more things that have changed and so have different implications compared to first editions, those are simply the ones that came to mind immediatly.<br /> <br /> In short: seemingly small changes have staggering implications that it may be opportune to consider.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2547,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","user":"Elderand","date":". 12-24-2014, 12:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","name":"Elderand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T21:47:41-08:00","id":348794,"title":"","content":"A lot of those implications might not have been in VtR 1e's core book, but the direction of the game line has been moving towards most of the implications in things over the years. I think how jarring the changes are, are somewhat dependent on comparing core book to core book, vs. seeing 2e as part of a continuum of changes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T22:02:57-08:00","id":348797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=348794#post348794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of those implications might not have been in VtR 1e's core book, but the direction of the game line has been moving towards most of the implications in things over the years. I think how jarring the changes are, are somewhat dependent on comparing core book to core book, vs. seeing 2e as part of a continuum of changes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> True, my point was more to emphasize that there have been changes that may have more implications than is apparent at first reading and so that backward compatibility may not be as straightforward as it seems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","name":"Elderand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T01:04:23-08:00","id":348884,"title":"","content":"I think a lot of those &quot;implications&quot; are not so implicit as you make them out to be. At the end of the day, there is always a Storyteller calling the shots, and if they don't want those changes to impact the way Kindred society functions, they don't impact the way Kindred Society functions. Tabletop games are cool like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T06:55:11-08:00","id":349031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=348884#post348884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a lot of those &quot;implications&quot; are not so implicit as you make them out to be. At the end of the day, there is always a Storyteller calling the shots, and if they don't want those changes to impact the way Kindred society functions, they don't impact the way Kindred Society functions. Tabletop games are cool like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure the ST can ignore anything it wants, nothing forces anyone to play anything in any way. But better awareness of potential issues does lead to better resolution.<br /> <br /> But none of this is entirely relevant to the question at hand.<br /> Backward compatibility.<br /> <br /> What's backward compatible ? Mechanicly wise a lot is unless it depends on subsystem that have been changed. And some old rules are essentialy obsolete and it's the little thing that catch you by surprise.<br /> Mythos wise I'd say compatibility is broad stroke only. A lot of little things have changed and make 1 for 1 port difficult at best. <br /> And sometimes, in re-examining things you find stuff that make you go &quot;well that's interesting, what if ?&quot; and now you have a wicked story hook to explore, or fun brain teaser.<br /> <br /> One exemple that happened to me not long ago.<br /> <br /> My player was a member of the ordo dracul and for unrelated reasons I was looking at the strix. So as I was brushing up on my ordo knowledge and seeing what fluff wise need to be updated my brain did a funny thing.<br /> <br /> It said this: &quot;Wait a minute, a lot of Dracula story as told in the old books can be seen through the lens of Dracula having been a strix !&quot;<br /> My gut reaction was of course to go &quot;no way!&quot; and ignore it. But then the potential dawned on me. The order does track the number of sireless embrace, of course most will just be about a clueless abandonned neonate or accident, but surely a number of these are the result of strix using synthesis on a corpse or living being. What if dracula was one of them ?<br /> But dracula said he talked to god, well, with the discovery that the whole out of body experience/tunnel of light thing can be replicated by using certain drugs, drugs that are produced by a dying brain, that certainly would rattle the position of traditionalist in the order. <br /> So what if some in the order realised the &quot;truth&quot; (whether it is true or not is up to the ST, but a faction may certainly believe so) an heresy whithin that seek to develop coils that turn vampires into strix.<br /> What if dracula was a strix and sook to develop method to corrupt vampires or make the beast inside burgeon into a full blownstrix ? It certainly make sense given the nature of the coil looking quite like what happen when a strix is possessing a vampire. At least superficialy.<br /> And in a domain where strix are present and everyone is paranoid about them, maybe the order doesn't advertise dracula story too much because then someone might get the wrong idea and start a witch hunt.<br /> <br /> The point is, there is a lot of potential to be found when updating things and there is fun to be had in not simply ignoring implications and do the same thing you've been doing since 1st.<br /> <br /> You can take a wild stab at exploring those new implications, maybe it work, maybe it doesn't. Or you can ignore those implications and maybe it works, maybe it blow up in your face when a player point at something and goes &quot;that doesn't make sense&quot;<br /> <br /> I think it's worth exploring even if in the end you decide to ignore the implications if you don't like them, at least you'll do so with the full knowledge of what could be.<br /> In short, don't knock it till you try it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","name":"Elderand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T07:59:19-08:00","id":349057,"title":"","content":"On the Mekhet point: Who says Mekhet let everyone know how much they can learn and how easily they can learn it? Secrets are their stock and trade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T21:41:45-08:00","id":349539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=349057#post349057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the Mekhet point: Who says Mekhet let everyone know how much they can learn and how easily they can learn it? Secrets are their stock and trade.</div> </div> </div> </div>The first time some Mekhet reveals that they know something they shouldn't, becomes sufficient excuse for some Ventrue to use Dominate to extract how they learned that fact, provide excruciating detail on how their power works, and if the Mekhet is lucky, then only the memories of every detail they obtained by mindraping that Ventrue of <i>their</i> memories is something they forget forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":190,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","user":"Audrey St. John","date":". 12-25-2014, 12:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T05:27:21-08:00","id":349791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This in turn affect kindred view of history. History is no longer this unknowable thing that can't be relied upon. Now it's a thing that should be doubted a little but since not everyone suffer from the fog of ages it can be argued that at least in the broad strokes history as the vampires knows it may be correct. There is a seed of doubt, but that's just that a seed. </div> </div> </div>I don't think that's necessarily true. The Kindred are still a very small highly secretive society prone to cataclysmic episodes of violence, that's really not an environment for keeping good history. Further, while they don't have the Fog of Ages, they don't have supernatural memory either. They're going to forget a lot of stuff, or at least radically alter it to fit the way they are now. I mean, vampires now radically change when they arise after a long torpor; that's going to mess with their memories of the past.<br /> <br /> I actually thought the Fog of Ages was really unnecessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T05:37:14-08:00","id":349792,"title":"","content":"Major thing is &quot;Its no longer Maquerade with a twist, but its own unique thing&quot;<br /> <br /> For better or for worse.<br /> <br /> They Axed Golconda as I previously mentioned.<br /> <br /> And as MIchael says the lack of fog of eternity, radicaly changes things.<br /> <br /> I really liked the theme of the elder waking up not knowing who he is, or being brainwashed by Someone else, possibly an enemy who captured and brainwashed him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T05:38:40-08:00","id":349793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=348785#post348785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> <br /> Clan weaknesses have changed, making the way everyone belonging to each clan act differently from what was happening in 1st edition, somtime drasticly so.<br /> Gangrel used to be...well...somewhat dumb. Now they just have a harder time resisting frenzy. They shouldn't be seen as dumb but potentialy very dangerous, not entirely out of control, they can guide their frenzy just as well as anyone else but they will frenzy more often.</div> </div> </div> </div>The 1st edition Gangral were not dumb. We ran it as they were restless and had ADHD.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Daeva were big vice indulgers, turning hedonistic out of necessity, now they they get a pseudo blood bond if they feed more than once from the same person, that makes them either supremely promscuous or supremely careful. </div> </div> </div> This is one of the ones I'm not sure about. Thematically I like the old Daeva Bane. May hack vice back do to that. <br /> Mask and Dirge remind me too much of Nature and Demeanor.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ventrue were prone to insanity, now they just have slightly more trouble with touchstones (it seems to be the conscencus that their clan weakness is a joke) </div> </div> </div>That is the other one that bothers me. I like the control freaks losing control of themselves. Strikes me as very gothic. And since I want to keep Malkavia it fits. I may retcon that as well<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T13:53:12-08:00","id":350039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Audrey St. John</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=349539#post349539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first time some Mekhet reveals that they know something they shouldn't, becomes sufficient excuse for some Ventrue to use Dominate to extract how they learned that fact, provide excruciating detail on how their power works, and if the Mekhet is lucky, then only the memories of every detail they obtained by mindraping that Ventrue of <i>their</i> memories is something they forget forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>So a Ventrue can just order you to spill all your secrets and make you forget about it afterward with two dots of Dominate, but we're supposed to be terrified of Mekhet in case they have Auspex 4?<br /> <br /> Sure, Mekhet are good at what they do, but I'm not seeing &quot;they should be treated like pariahs or killed on sight&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=349791#post349791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Further, while they don't have the Fog of Ages, they don't have supernatural memory either. They're going to forget a lot of stuff, or at least radically alter it to fit the way they are now. [...] I actually thought the Fog of Ages was really unnecessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>True that. How detailed are your memories of thirty years ago? How <b>exact</b> are they? Can you remember the name of that one coworker who screwed you over, or even what the heck the whole deal was even about? Now remind me again why you need some sort of fancy supernatural effect to justify &quot;elder vampires can't remember very well what happened <i>two thousand years ago</i>&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":815,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","user":"Kazorh","date":". 12-25-2014, 05:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T21:40:27-08:00","id":350390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Audrey St. John</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=349539#post349539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The first time some Mekhet reveals that they know something they shouldn't, becomes sufficient excuse for some Ventrue to use Dominate to extract how they learned that fact, provide excruciating detail on how their power works, and if the Mekhet is lucky, then only the memories of every detail they obtained by mindraping that Ventrue of <i>their</i> memories is something they forget forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any Kindred who drops blackmail on another is either typically prepared for the blacklash that it is bound to create or simply not long for this world. Dropping baggage on a Venture one vs one in a back alley is completely different than say doing it at an Elysium. Allies need to be accounted for, Assets need to be called, etc. Given the social opera of Kindred, Actions and powers have tangible social effects. The Venture could ignore the Mekhat and the patrons will simply wonder if the Mekhat is correct or not. The Venture can mind rape the Mekhat and now all the patrons know the dirt that the Mekhat was valid and start acting accordingly.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T22:22:10-08:00","id":350430,"title":"","content":"I think people may be getting too focused on the specific exemple, so let's broaden things up.<br /> <br /> The point was that mekhets would keep secret how easily they can, well, find out secrets. And it seems on the surface to be reasonable, but if you dig just a little deeper it start straining credulity.<br /> <br /> For this to be true you have to make an astounding number of assumptions. First Mehkets never tell anyone, seems the most reasonable, except they are a clan, which are far less controlled than covenants are. Even covenant secrets gets out from time to time. Leaks happen just because of basic human nature.<br /> Second. Mekhet never have shared, willingly or not, their gift with anyone else. <br /> <br /> Over the entire history of vampire kind, never has a mekhet spilled the bean, cracked under torture, been dominated or charmed into speaking, been diablerized by a blabber mouth, shared secrets with a covennats or coterie member. Spontaneous (real or strix induced) embrace of mekhets never was lacking in judgement, never has a strix just dropped the bomb of what mekhet can do just for shit and giggle to instigate distrust.<br /> <br /> It just take one good exemple of one of these things to spread the knowledge that mekhets can just look at you and play twenty questions in their head and suddenly they know all your dirty little secrets.<br /> The alternative is that Mekhets are super organized and policed clan of unbreakable badasses that never show any weakness, get possessed or diablerize or who manage to eliminate every trace of the knowledge when it's spilled.<br /> <br /> All of this has huge implications for Mekhets that the book just doesn't explore. And it can be fun to explore them. It doesn't have to end up in Mekhet being exterminated but that's a possibility. There are countless others. But applying the previous relationship and position of the status quo of the previous edition to this one when things have changed so dramaticly ? Well, you can if you want, but personaly I find it hard to swallow.<br /> <br /> And it is a problem that is highly exacerbated in the case of auspex. Pretty much everything else has a countermeasure somewhere, be it opposed rolls, lashing out, merits blocking or what have you. Auspex just work, the countermesure seems to be that you can get false information but any Mekhet worth his salt will test several time and corroborate through other means once he become awares false information is a possibility. And since the false information is matter for the ST and not for the person being observed, you can't even really plant false trails in the hope a mekhet will pick up on that false information. The false info he get could be entirely different to the false trail you prepared. So for all intent and purpose there is no real defense against a mekhet finding out your secrets.<br /> <br /> Unless you have access to blood sorcery and have protection 4 as a theme. Then you may be protected. And if you don't have access to blood sorcery, you need to find someone who does and convince them to help you and then you have to trust them to actually protect you and not lay a curse or use this opportunity to find out the very secrets you wanted protected.<br /> <br /> Mind you my point is not that it was wrong to do auspex the way it was done, but that the implications of it could have been explored more. Which for now is up to indicidual ST. I do hope the subject get explored more deeply in future books. It would be a shame to ignore the potential there for the sake of maintaining some sort of status quo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","name":"Elderand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T00:03:07-08:00","id":350506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=350430#post350430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point was that mekhets would keep secret how easily they can, well, find out secrets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I think you'll find that my point was that a Ventrue can find out secrets just as easily and yet nobody is talking about the implications that vampires would treat as pariahs the clan that can find out all your secrets <i>and also turn you into a puppet</i>.<br /> <br /> Besides, if you want to find out all of someone's secrets, you really need Lay Open the Mind, which IS contested. Uncanny Perception is awesome, but it has some fundamental limitations. It's just not going to give you the detailed explanation of your target's plot to overthrow the Prince.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T01:59:28-08:00","id":350528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=350430#post350430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For this to be true you have to make an astounding number of assumptions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't this exactly what you're doing? You're basically assuming everything as strongly as possible towards your interpretation, even if things under discussion are variable<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It just take one good exemple of one of these things to spread the knowledge that mekhets can just look at you and play twenty questions in their head and suddenly they know all your dirty little secrets. </div> </div> </div>All of the Clan signature Disciplines are scary and you don't want them used against you. Vampires are powerful. Vampires have always been portrayed in Requiem as being a contradiction in terms of socializing with each other. Other vampires have always been a threat, but a source of power and safety at the same time. Lone vampires don't have to deal with vampires that have powers they can't do anything about, or the politics, but they also don't have anyone else to helping to keep their domains safe and secure against outsiders, hunters, Strix, and everything else that's a problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But applying the previous relationship and position of the status quo of the previous edition to this one when things have changed so dramaticly ? Well, you can if you want, but personaly I find it hard to swallow. </div> </div> </div>I think many of us aren't buying this idea that Auspex has radically changed so drastically. Auspex in 1e and 2e both allows Mekhet to do something scary: find out shit about you. &quot;20 questions&quot; is different from &quot;Aura of vague colors,&quot; but ultimately the &quot;threat&quot; Mekhet pose as information gatherers is the same. One sitting around watching you for long enough is going to learn things about you that you'd rather they didn't know.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Pretty much everything else has a countermeasure somewhere, be it opposed rolls, lashing out, merits blocking or what have you. </div> </div> </div>Um... why don't Lashing Out or Clash of Wills function as couter-measures?<br /> <br /> If your Mekhet is sitting around staring at my Gangrel intently... why can't my Gangrel Lash Out to make sure that they stop and end that little attempt to invade is mind?<br /> <br /> If my Ventrue used Dominate to mess with his Ghoul's memories, why wouldn't your Mekhet have to beat my Ventrue in a Clash of Wills to get at the real ones?<br /> <br /> What are the countermeasures to stop another vampires from using Protean, Vigor, Celerity, Resilience, Animalism.... well you get the idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So for all intent and purpose there is no real defense against a mekhet finding out your secrets. </div> </div> </div>And? This isn't new. Auspex allowed that before<br /> <br /> As well, there's a big difference between a Mekhet knowing your secrets and being about to do anything about it. It isn't actually proof after all. It's not evidence they can give to somebody to blackmail you with. If a Mekhet accuses you of diablerie but you were smart and made sure to cover it up well, you get to just call them a liar and have them come up with some evidence rather than claiming mystic mumbo jumbo as fact. Any vampire that trusts the Mekhet has to acknowledge to themselves that this means the Mekhet is going around scanning people for things to make accusations about and they aren't going to want to be next; so they'll want loud mouthed Mekhet out of the picture. As will everyone that doesn't want to put up with a Mekhet trying to use Auspex based accusations to control the domain.<br /> <br /> Knowledge may be power, but power is meaningless without a way to use it. A gun with no bullets might be good for a bluff, but it isn't an effective weapon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T08:02:13-08:00","id":350658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=349791#post349791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think that's necessarily true. The Kindred are still a very small highly secretive society prone to cataclysmic episodes of violence, that's really not an environment for keeping good history. Further, <b>while they don't have the Fog of Ages, they don't have supernatural memory either.</b> They're going to forget a lot of stuff, or at least radically alter it to fit the way they are now. I mean, vampires now radically change when they arise after a long torpor; that's going to mess with their memories of the past.<br /> <br /> I actually thought the Fog of Ages was really unnecessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Supernatural Memory is not needed. The existence of the Merits <i><b>Eidetic Memory </b></i>or <i><b>Trained Memory </b></i>get past the need for that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T08:13:35-08:00","id":350662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Supernatural Memory is not needed. The existence of the Merits <i><b>Eidetic Memory </b></i>or <i><b>Trained Memory </b></i>get past the need for that. <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> </div> </div> </div>I can't tell if that's a joke or you're actually serious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T08:37:44-08:00","id":350670,"title":"","content":"A little of both, actually. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> When you do not have to roll to remember anything that you have experienced (unless you are under stress), it is a pretty powerful thing, given you can live for thousands of years, if you are careful.<br /> <br /> Never really been a big issue in our games (I do not use Fog of Ages for Vampires in 1E), but the potential for vast stores of accurate knowledge is there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 12-26-2014, 11:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T08:37:52-08:00","id":350671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=350528#post350528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't this exactly what you're doing? You're basically assuming everything as strongly as possible towards your interpretation, even if things under discussion are variable</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, let's see. One side assume that mekhet works perfectly, never slip up, never crack under pressure, that no one ever aqucire auspex through teaching diablerie or bloodline and that this has been going on for all of kindred history. <br /> I assume mistakes will be made somewhere down the line.<br /> <br /> Yes, clearly both set of assumption are just as strong and equal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think many of us aren't buying this idea that Auspex has radically changed so drastically. Auspex in 1e and 2e both allows Mekhet to do something scary: find out shit about you. &quot;20 questions&quot; is different from &quot;Aura of vague colors,&quot; but ultimately the &quot;threat&quot; Mekhet pose as information gatherers is the same. One sitting around watching you for long enough is going to learn things about you that you'd rather they didn't know. </div> </div> </div>There is a large qualitative difference between knowing someone's mood, but not what caused said mood, and knowing their secrets in details. Yes if you reduce it enough it becomes &quot;something you don't want them to know&quot; Just like if you reduce it enough slightly moldy cheese and uranium can be reduced to stuff you don't want to put in your mouth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Um... why don't Lashing Out or Clash of Wills function as couter-measures? </div> </div> </div>Clash of will may work in some corner cases, Lashing out won't do squat, wanton and Bestial don't do anything and competitive doesn't apply because, funny that, auspex is neither contested or resisted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If your Mekhet is sitting around staring at my Gangrel intently... why can't my Gangrel Lash Out to make sure that they stop and end that little attempt to invade is mind? </div> </div> </div>Except he isn't staring intently, he is glancing your way for a few seconds, probably when you have your back turned. And if you're going to lash out everytime a Mekhet glances your way, why it's almost like Mekhets are pariahs that should keep their eyes firmly on the ground or risk being kicked to the curb.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If my Ventrue used Dominate to mess with his Ghoul's memories, why wouldn't your Mekhet have to beat my Ventrue in a Clash of Wills to get at the real ones? </div> </div> </div>It would, but it's a corner case and a mekhet going after a ghoul of a know ventrue will, if he is smart, ask if the memories have been messed around with. You may hide the specifics but you can't cover your cover up as easily as you would with anyone else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What are the countermeasures to stop another vampires from using Protean, Vigor, Celerity, Resilience, Animalism.... well you get the idea. </div> </div> </div>Using most disciplines as a comparaison is really mixing apple and oranges. The countermeasures, are going to be resisted or contested rolls, dodging, using other disciplines to counter the effects and so on. Very little of which ever applies to Auspex.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And? This isn't new. Auspex allowed that before<br /> <br /> As well, there's a big difference between a Mekhet knowing your secrets and being about to do anything about it. It isn't actually proof after all. It's not evidence they can give to somebody to blackmail you with. If a Mekhet accuses you of diablerie but you were smart and made sure to cover it up well, you get to just call them a liar and have them come up with some evidence rather than claiming mystic mumbo jumbo as fact. Any vampire that trusts the Mekhet has to acknowledge to themselves that this means the Mekhet is going around scanning people for things to make accusations about and they aren't going to want to be next; so they'll want loud mouthed Mekhet out of the picture. As will everyone that doesn't want to put up with a Mekhet trying to use Auspex based accusations to control the domain.<br /> <br /> Knowledge may be power, but power is meaningless without a way to use it. A gun with no bullets might be good for a bluff, but it isn't an effective weapon. </div> </div> </div>And again you're just giving an exemple of mekhets as social pariahs that no one want to listen to or aknowledge, more than ready to turn violent when one of them says anything that hints at their abilities. This is different from what I said how ? I'm being a little hyperbolic admitedly but you get the idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=350506#post350506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I think you'll find that my point was that a Ventrue can find out secrets just as easily and yet nobody is talking about the implications that vampires would treat as pariahs the clan that can find out all your secrets <i>and also turn you into a puppet</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mekhet was just one exemple I've given, one that everyone latched on because I said it was one of the biggest change. Beside, while dominate is scary but it's very nature it limits itself and make itself extremely easy to get out of if you're even slightly prepared. Against any vampire the very first command you need to give them is don't hurt yourself, or they can just break a finger or something similar to resolve mesmerized, and if you do use that command then they are free to attack you. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Besides, if you want to find out all of someone's secrets, you really need Lay Open the Mind, which IS contested. Uncanny Perception is awesome, but it has some fundamental limitations. It's just not going to give you the detailed explanation of your target's plot to overthrow the Prince. </div> </div> </div>Lay open the mind is the fast brute force way to find things out. But Uncanny perception, time and some smart question is all you need to produce exactly the same result, hence why I qualified it as 20 questions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","name":"Elderand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T08:38:01-08:00","id":350672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Audrey St. John</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=349539#post349539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> mindraping</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=350390#post350390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">mind rape</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:red\">Lets not use the word rape so casually, please.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T11:48:08-08:00","id":350813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=350671#post350671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mekhet was just one exemple I've given, one that everyone latched on because I said it was one of the biggest change.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which doesn't particularly matter for my points, since I've never said anything for or against your general point that there are a lot of new assumptions. All I did was see someone saying that the Mekhet clan couldn't possibly keep Auspex as anything resembling a secret, because a Ventrue could just trivially Dominate you into spilling everything. At which point I noted that saying Ventrues are so good at getting your secrets out of you goes against the idea that Mekhet would be treated like pariahs for exactly the same reason.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=350671#post350671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beside, while dominate is scary but it's very nature it limits itself and make itself extremely easy to get out of if you're even slightly prepared. Against any vampire the very first command you need to give them is don't hurt yourself, or they can just break a finger or something similar to resolve mesmerized, and if you do use that command then they are free to attack you.</div> </div> </div> </div>That... Okay, that's not how I've ever ran Dominate. When someone has applied the Mesmerized Condition on you, you've just been hypnotized. You calm the heck down and listen to orders. You don't immediately break your own finger and you don't start punching the Ventrue either (unless a friendly Ventrue gave you an Entombed Command to do exactly that, granted). Even then, though, just use &quot;don't move&quot; as your first order.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=350671#post350671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lay open the mind is the fast brute force way to find things out. But Uncanny perception, time and some smart question is all you need to produce exactly the same result, hence why I qualified it as 20 questions.</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to be overestimating it. Uncanny Perception will tell you that Elder X is envious of the Prince and has violent feelings toward them, and that he's sleeping with Confederate Y. It's never going to tell you that Elder X and Confederate Y are planning to diablerize the Prince on Monday night at 2 a.m. Auspex 4 and Dominate 2 will tell you exactly that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T12:11:13-08:00","id":350824,"title":"","content":"I think one side of this argument is grossly overstating the detail at which Auspex gives information. Let's say, if I were pissed at vampire X, for doing bad things to my ghoul the auspex would at best discern that&quot;I am pissed at vampire X&quot;, that &quot;my ghoul is my ghoul&quot; probably that &quot;my ghoul is afraid of vampire X&quot;. That's as much detail as you're gonna get without Auspex 4. I'd like to say that it's not much detail at all. And with Auspex 4, nothing changed there, old Auspex 4 was even more powerful then the current version is. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T12:48:09-08:00","id":350856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=350671#post350671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One side assume that mekhet works perfectly, never slip up, never crack under pressure, that no one ever aqucire auspex through teaching diablerie or bloodline and that this has been going on for all of kindred history.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pointless strawment are pointless.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I assume mistakes will be made somewhere down the line. </div> </div> </div>No, you're making a lot bigger assumptions down the line. Like Mekhet's all use Auspex, and all use Auspex to its maximum effect all the time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is a large qualitative difference between knowing someone's mood, but not what caused said mood, and knowing their secrets in details. </div> </div> </div>Details takes time and effort (and possibly a lot of vitae). That's one of the big things about Aupsex 2 you're making assumptions about. The character has to know what they're looking for, or they're going fishing. Fishing takes a lot of time and/or blood, and never guarantees you ask the right questions to get what you want. Once you're talking about a Mekhet spying on someone for an extended period of time, compare it to actual mortal investigation abilities and... it's not actually that much better. If you're going to take a week to look into another vampire's activities Auspex is great, but good investigation skills can uncover all sorts of things (and come in all sorts of forms besides Auspex).<br /> <br /> [quoteYes if you reduce it enough it becomes &quot;something you don't want them to know&quot; Just like if you reduce it enough slightly moldy cheese and uranium can be reduced to stuff you don't want to put in your mouth.[/quote]<br /> <br /> This is actual apples to oranges.<br /> <br /> One thing you're ignoring about the difference between Auspex 2 1e and Auspex 2 2e is that in 1e you can just scan people and the power tells you interesting things about them. It generates useful information without any forethought by the character. In 2e the character actually have to be looking for specific things. In 2e you have to have questions that matter, or spend a lot of time/vitae spamming questions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Clash of will may work in some corner cases, Lashing out won't do squat, wanton and Bestial don't do anything and competitive doesn't apply because, funny that, auspex is neither contested or resisted. </div> </div> </div>Clash of Wills will apply to any time you try to use Auspex to uncover information being hidden by Disciplines. It's only &quot;some corner cases&quot; if all the other vampires on earth are idiots and don't use their Disciplines to help hide any of their secrets.<br /> <br /> I think you're also misinterpreting how Lashing Out functions as a defense against Disciplines. It's not about directly opposing Disciplines, it's about compelling actions in the other vampire by drawing out their Beast.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Except he isn't staring intently, he is glancing your way for a few seconds, probably when you have your back turned. </div> </div> </div>So assumption is that all Mekhet are experts at covertly staring at people and never get noticed. Noted and dismissed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And if you're going to lash out everytime a Mekhet glances your way, why it's almost like Mekhets are pariahs that should keep their eyes firmly on the ground or risk being kicked to the curb. </div> </div> </div>Staring at other vampires is, generally speaking, probably fairly rude given Auspex and Dominate. As well, spending ~3 seconds during a conversation involving a group of people staring at anybody that isn't holding the floor for that long is fairly noticeable behavior.<br /> <br /> Mekhet that are obtrusive with their powers are pariahs <i>just like any other vampire that leans too heavily on their Disciplines with other vampires</i>. A Ventrue that Dominates their way through all of their kindred issues is going to get stigmatized for it. A Daeva that uses Majesty all the time to be socially unassailable is going to have the same problems.<br /> <br /> Mekhet aren't special in this regard. Nobody likes a vampire that throws their Discplines around all the time at other vampires. The only thing that separates out the Mekhet is that their signature Discipline is the most subtle of the five. But it all comes down to how a vampire uses their powers rather than the changes from 1e to 2e radically altering anything in vampire politics and society.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It would, but it's a corner case and a mekhet going after a ghoul of a know ventrue will, if he is smart, ask if the memories have been messed around with. </div> </div> </div>When the majority of things are corner cases, it makes me think that you don't know what a corner case is. A Ventrue's mortal servants have had their memories messed with is a corner case? Sorry, but no, that's something that should fairly common place really. Wasting an Auspex 2 question on that is like using Auspex 3 to ask the road if the sky is blue in the day. Knowing that someone's memories have been messed with doesn't stop them from needing to beat a Clash of Wills to get around it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Using most disciplines as a comparaison is really mixing apple and oranges. </div> </div> </div>Then your own point is irrelevant. You compared 2e Auspex to other Disciplines by comparing how easy you perceive them to be countered. You can't cherry pick how to compare Disciplines. Either we get to compare them, or we don't. Arbitrarily excluding lots of Disciplines because it makes your point weaker is transparent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And again you're just giving an exemple of mekhets as social pariahs that no one want to listen to or aknowledge, more than ready to turn violent when one of them says anything that hints at their abilities. This is different from what I said how ? I'm being a little hyperbolic admitedly but you get the idea. </div> </div> </div>The difference is that in my example the problem is <b>the Mekhet is being an idiot</b> by assuming that knowing something is the same as proof.<br /> <br /> Knowing things by itself is actually not that powerful. You have to be able to leverage knowledge to make it do something for you.<br /> <br /> <b>All</b> vampires that try to control other vampires via Disciplines are making themselves outcasts and pariahs because nobody wants to deal with that ass. Clan is irrelevant. That's my point here. Having potent powers only makes you a pariah if you use them like an idiot (or even just threaten to).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T13:03:45-08:00","id":350864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A little of both, actually. <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> When you do not have to roll to remember anything that you have experienced (unless you are under stress), it is a pretty powerful thing, given you can live for thousands of years, if you are careful. </div> </div> </div>I'm speechless.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T13:25:19-08:00","id":350873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=350864#post350864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm speechless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would that impart speechlessness? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T13:43:45-08:00","id":350879,"title":"","content":"The wording of eidetic memory suggest to me, that it's meant for ease of use in play; buying it meaning you don't need to tiresomely write everything down. Further, from it not being a supernatural merit, it's supposed to be something an actual person could reasonably be expected to have. Therefore it probably just means you have a particularly good memory.<br /> <br /> However, read literally, it does indeed seem to mean the character has a magically perfect memory. I am just surpised anyone would interpret it that way; hence my speechlessness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T13:46:49-08:00","id":350881,"title":"","content":"The difference between a particularly good memory and someone who truly has an Eidetic (read photographic) memory (I have met a couple of them - real people who are preternaturally able to recall anything they have ever witnessed... it is creepy as hell, to be honest) is a really, really fine line. The fact of the Merit's existence means someone will use them in the game for exactly what I described (again, seen it a time or two). To be honest, it is not really all that problematic, in my experience, but it may be a bit annoying to others. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 12-26-2014, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T13:51:19-08:00","id":350882,"title":"","content":"In my experience, Uncanny Perception is functionally almost identical to Aura Perception, it's just more transparent about how it works. I don't know about anyone else, but I could never learn all of those aura colors and what they meant, and I didn't expect my players to memorize them, so we always just had the Auspex user just ask questions anyway. &quot;What emotion is this character feeling most strongly right now?&quot; or &quot;does this character's aura have Diablerie stains?&quot; or what have you. Second Edition just decided to quit beating around the bush and just tell the player to to ask questions and the storyteller to answer in symbolic imagery. Honestly, when I read 2E Auspex, I saw the exact same list of powers, just written in a less obtuse way. The only thing that really changed in a significant way was the first dot, all the other changes were just for ease of use and clarity of mechanical function.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 12-26-2014, 04:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T14:06:24-08:00","id":350906,"title":"","content":"Why just single out Mekhet? I counted 14 (1st edition) non Mekhet bloodlines with auspex. Even signature disciplines get around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ortam + Malkavia makes a Requiem fun.<br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Posts in this colour are Persuasion.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">Posts in this colour are Seduction.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this colour are Intimidation.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/57-solomon-birch","name":"solomon birch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar57_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T14:08:39-08:00","id":350910,"title":"","content":"Well, there is &quot;getting around&quot; and then there is Auspex standing on a corner propositioning other Bloodlines. ...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T15:44:16-08:00","id":350992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=350879#post350879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The wording of eidetic memory suggest to me, that it's meant for ease of use in play; buying it meaning you don't need to tiresomely write everything down. Further, from it not being a supernatural merit, it's supposed to be something an actual person could reasonably be expected to have. Therefore it probably just means you have a particularly good memory.<br /> <br /> However, read literally, it does indeed seem to mean the character has a magically perfect memory. I am just surpised anyone would interpret it that way; hence my speechlessness.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.slate.com/articles/health_and_science/science/2006/04/kaavya_syndrome.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://dot.cdnslate.com/static/media/sites/slate-com/icon.400x400.09ec623.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.slate.com/articles/health_and_science/science/2006/04/kaavya_syndrome.html\" target=\"_blank\"> No one has a photographic memory. </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.slate.com/articles/health_and_science/science/2006/04/kaavya_syndrome.html\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.slate.com/articles/health_and_science/science/2006/04/kaavya_syndrome.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Kaavya Viswanathan has an excuse. In this morning's New York Times, the author of How Opal Mehta Got Kissed, Got Wild, and Got a Life explained how... </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eidetic_memory\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/static/images/icons/enwiki-25.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eidetic_memory\" target=\"_blank\"> Eidetic memory - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eidetic_memory\" target=\"_blank\"> http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eidetic_memory </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T17:37:35-08:00","id":351108,"title":"","content":"And yet people with extraordinary memory do exist (I have met a few), though exactly HOW FAR that memory persists is somewhat debatable. Regardless, I have met a few people who have that sort of memory recall and it is really creepy. Call it what you will... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 12-26-2014, 08:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T17:57:24-08:00","id":351117,"title":"","content":"Creepier if they remember Caligula.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ortam + Malkavia makes a Requiem fun.<br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Posts in this colour are Persuasion.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">Posts in this colour are Seduction.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this colour are Intimidation.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/57-solomon-birch","name":"solomon birch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar57_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T21:47:42-08:00","id":351327,"title":"","content":"I wonder if the second edition of M:tAw will have that one Mind spell that lets you remember something perfectly, forever. I think it was in the Mysterium book? I once reflected on how it'd make a weird prank to pull on a vampire. Burn a false assertion into their mind, and a thousand years later all the details of that time period will be so muddled in their memories they'll probably assume whatever lie you told them is actually the truth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T07:02:16-08:00","id":352629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=350992#post350992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.slate.com/articles/health_and_science/science/2006/04/kaavya_syndrome.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://dot.cdnslate.com/static/media/sites/slate-com/icon.400x400.09ec623.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.slate.com/articles/health_and_science/science/2006/04/kaavya_syndrome.html\" target=\"_blank\"> No one has a photographic memory. </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.slate.com/articles/health_and_science/science/2006/04/kaavya_syndrome.html\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.slate.com/articles/health_and_science/science/2006/04/kaavya_syndrome.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Kaavya Viswanathan has an excuse. In this morning's New York Times, the author of How Opal Mehta Got Kissed, Got Wild, and Got a Life explained how... </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eidetic_memory\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/static/images/icons/enwiki-25.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eidetic_memory\" target=\"_blank\"> Eidetic memory - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eidetic_memory\" target=\"_blank\"> http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eidetic_memory </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>This part from the slate article is debatable (bold is mine):<br /> <br /> &quot;A group of Talmudic scholars known as the Shass Pollaks supposedly stored mental snapshots of all 5,422 pages of the Babylonian Talmud. According to a paper published in 1917 in the journal Psychological Review, psychologist George Stratton tested the Shass Pollaks by sticking a pin through various tractates of the Talmud. They responded by telling him exactly which words the pin passed through on every page. In fact, the Shass Pollaks probably didn't possess photographic memory so much as heroic perseverance. If the average person decided he was going to dedicate his entire life to memorizing 5,422 pages of text, he'd probably also be pretty good at it. <b>It's an impressive feat of single-mindedness, not of memory.</b>&quot;<br /> <br /> How is that not an impressive feat of memory? Weird conclusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T10:27:09-08:00","id":352829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=352629#post352629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This part from the slate article is debatable (bold is mine):<br /> <br /> &quot;A group of Talmudic scholars known as the Shass Pollaks supposedly stored mental snapshots of all 5,422 pages of the Babylonian Talmud. According to a paper published in 1917 in the journal Psychological Review, psychologist George Stratton tested the Shass Pollaks by sticking a pin through various tractates of the Talmud. They responded by telling him exactly which words the pin passed through on every page. In fact, the Shass Pollaks probably didn't possess photographic memory so much as heroic perseverance. If the average person decided he was going to dedicate his entire life to memorizing 5,422 pages of text, he'd probably also be pretty good at it. <b>It's an impressive feat of single-mindedness, not of memory.</b>&quot;<br /> <br /> How is that not an impressive feat of memory? Weird conclusion.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point the author is making is that while, obviously, remembering a whole book involves memory, it doesn't actually show a superhuman memory on the part of those who did it, &quot;merely&quot; incredible single-mindedness. Which is why the preceding sentence talks about what &quot;the average person&quot; could do since the &quot;average person&quot; by definition has an average memory, not any sort of eidetic of perfect recall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T11:30:03-08:00","id":352907,"title":"","content":"I think anyone who dedicates their lives to memorizing 5,422 pages of text can no longer be accurately described as &quot;the average person.&quot;<br /> <br /> I mean, I get that what the author is trying to say is since anyone could theoretically train themselves to do that, it's more an example of what people are capable of when they apply themselves fully to something than it is an example of these people being gifted with superhuman memory. Still, calling it &quot;not [a feat] of memory&quot; is an odd word choice. It's more that it's a feat of trained memory not a feat of inborn menomic capabilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T15:06:58-08:00","id":353169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=350882#post350882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my experience, Uncanny Perception is functionally almost identical to Aura Perception, it's just more transparent about how it works. I don't know about anyone else, but I could never learn all of those aura colors and what they meant, and I didn't expect my players to memorize them, so we always just had the Auspex user just ask questions anyway. &quot;What emotion is this character feeling most strongly right now?&quot; or &quot;does this character's aura have Diablerie stains?&quot; or what have you. Second Edition just decided to quit beating around the bush and just tell the player to to ask questions and the storyteller to answer in symbolic imagery. Honestly, when I read 2E Auspex, I saw the exact same list of powers, just written in a less obtuse way. The only thing that really changed in a significant way was the first dot, all the other changes were just for ease of use and clarity of mechanical function.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe superficially. Auspex 2 does a lot more than just read emotions. Psychological vulnerabilities, vice/dirge, &quot;who here does this person want to hurt the most&quot;... these things couldn't be done with the old Auspex. And that's just from the sample questions. Going by the power's description you can make a lot of other interesting questions as well. &quot;Is this person lying to me?&quot; for instance. With aura reading you could maybe see someone get nervous, but not everyone gets nervous while telling a lie, and a lot of other people get nervous just by being asked weird questions, even when they're being truthful. It doesn't matter what they feel like now, though.<br /> <br /> No, I don't think calling it functionally identical to Aura Perception is fair at all.<br /> <br /> Apart from those first two, the other 3 are pretty similar to what we had before, yeah, but that's alright. They didn't change in theme much, but I do think they got better. Also, some Obfuscate changes are pretty neat coupled with Auspex. Familiar Stranger (now much improved) coupled with Lay Open The Mind makes you a perfect look alike while also allowing you to know exactly what the other person is expecting you to say on tricky questions. There's almost no chance of being found out at that point. Sure, you could just brute force dominate your way in a lot of places, but that leaves a trace. (And every power constantly runs into &quot;Well, you could do this with Dominate!&quot; anyway.)<br /> <br /> I like how we can go on a year long time skip, and I can hand the ST a list with questions I ask about every important NPC I meet regularly in that year, and get back an entire sheet with all of their masks, dirges, psychological vulnerabilities, greatest aspirations, etc... It's come in handy several times. Dominate could get the same secrets and more, but then the entire domain would likely be at war with me by the end of that year. You always fuck up somewhere, and dominate on that scale...<br /> <br /> And for those who say that you can just notice a Mekhet staring at you intently... &quot;Other vampires have no way to know when someone is using Auspex to discover their secrets.&quot; Plus it says you use the Beast's senses. It never says this sense has to be vision.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T16:17:05-08:00","id":353235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=353169#post353169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe superficially. Auspex 2 does a lot more than just read emotions. Psychological vulnerabilities, vice/dirge, &amp;quot;who here does this person want to hurt the most&amp;quot;... these things couldn't be done with the old Auspex. And that's just from the sample questions. Going by the power's description you can make a lot of other interesting questions as well. &amp;quot;Is this person lying to me?&amp;quot; for instance. With aura reading you could maybe see someone get nervous, but not everyone gets nervous while telling a lie, and a lot of other people get nervous just by being asked weird questions, even when they're being truthful. It doesn't matter what they feel like now, though.<br /> <br /> No, I don't think calling it functionally identical to Aura Perception is fair at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was being a little hyperbolic there, yes the potential uses for the powers have gotten a little more borad, but how much so is highly dependent on how liberally your ST interpreted the 1e versions. Personally, I always allowed Aura Perception to detect lies, as well as Virtue and Vice. I probably wouldn't have allowed &quot;who does this person want to hurt most?&quot; but a clever player would have been able to figure out the answer to that question on their own with a bit of Vitae and some deductive reasoning. I realize most people were probably a bit more conservative with Auspex than I was, but I still don't see the change as being nearly as big a difference as a lot of folks make it out to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T16:29:07-08:00","id":353240,"title":"","content":"In 1E Aura Perception allowed for Wits + Empathy + Auspex rolls for detecting lies... if that ain't a lie detector, I don't know what is, since that dice pool usually wins over anything thrown at it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T10:53:04-08:00","id":353868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=353240#post353240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 1E Aura Perception allowed for Wits + Empathy + Auspex rolls for detecting lies... if that ain't a lie detector, I don't know what is, since that dice pool usually wins over anything thrown at it.</div> </div> </div> </div>True that.<br /> <br /> On the topic of Auspex, anyone noticed auspex uses a ridiculous number of different skills and attributes compared to other disciplines? Luckily almost all of the dots get by on smaller dicepools than usual, but still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T11:57:32-08:00","id":353954,"title":"","content":"Aura Perception is actually better at detecting lies if the social scene takes a while, since you can use it all the time. There are only so many questions you can ask with Uncanny Perception without draining yourself of Vitae.<br /> <br /> Also, while it's true that Uncanny Perception can divine information that Aura Perception cannot, I take exception with the example that is being used. Consider this: &quot;Two successes might indicate that a ghoul swings from love to hate toward his mistress (bright blue to black), and is envious of a fellow ghoul (dark green).&quot; You have to take the dicepool penalty for &quot;subtle shifts in the mixtures of color and pattern&quot;, but Aura Perception can show relatively detailed information, including who is the target of the read person's emotion. It wouldn't be much of a stretch to ask &quot;who here does this person want to hurt most&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T14:27:04-08:00","id":354091,"title":"","content":"Eh, the entire rest of Aura Perception constantly stresses the &quot;right here, right now&quot; nature of the power. I've always interpreted that example as having to have said mistress and rival ghoul right there in the scene. You observe the mistress going close and see the flicker of the aura, then the other ghoul does something and you see the first guy's aura flicker, and you interpret all these signs. Since the example gives no context you -could- see it as aura perception not requiring the person to be present, but I don't see much support for that elsewhere. Also some questions might not be answerable due to the target's mood. If some guy is currently exploding in rage one of his more subtler emotions may not currently be detectable.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, with the new auspex 2 you can ask &quot;Who does this person mean harm the most?&quot; and get an answer no matter if the other person is present, what's happening right at that time, etc.<br /> <br /> Aura reading is better for sustained detection during a long scene though, I have to give it that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T16:01:08-08:00","id":354150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=354091#post354091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meanwhile, with the new auspex 2 you can ask &quot;Who does this person mean harm the most?&quot; and get an answer no matter if the other person is present, what's happening right at that time, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Er, no, you can't. The exact wording in the book is &quot;Who <b>here</b> does this person want to hurt most?&quot; and &quot;What is this person afraid of <b>right now</b>?&quot; Uncanny Perception lets you know stuff that's either immediately relevant (what they feel about people who are present) or an integral part of their person (being a diablerist or a supernatural creature). Same thing as Aura Perception, except you can also see Vice/Requiem.<br /> <br /> The examples bear it out: tasting bile while looking at someone or seeing a dagger pointing both involve the target of hate being present. &quot;Who here&quot; is also the same wording used with pretty much every example question for Beast's Hackles, and I don't think anyone is saying that Auspex 1 lets you know stuff about people or things that aren't present.<br /> <br /> The only way I'd allow it to tell you that they hate someone who isn't present would be if they were <i>obsessed</i> with that person on a level that reached &quot;psychiatric disorder&quot;, on par with the depression and schizophrenia that are the examples for psychological vulnerabilities.<br /> <br /> Edit: Somewhat unrelated: would you say Uncanny Perception can find out someone's Virtue? On one hand, that's definitely part of &quot;the truth underneath&quot;. On the other, Auspex has a bias for things like weakness, fear and loathing, while a Virtue is pretty positive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":815,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","user":"Kazorh","date":". 12-29-2014, 07:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T17:50:56-08:00","id":354206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=354150#post354150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: Somewhat unrelated: would you say Uncanny Perception can find out someone's Virtue? On one hand, that's definitely part of &quot;the truth underneath&quot;. On the other, Auspex has a bias for things like weakness, fear and loathing, while a Virtue is pretty positive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd allow it. Especially with the new approach to Virtue and Vice in second edition; they're no longer inherently positive or inherently negative traits, but things the character sees as positive or negative in herself. That's why things like &quot;Ambitious&quot; can be one character's Virtue and another character's Vice. I think you could easily present scanning for Virtue with Uncanny Perception as looking for what things cause the subject a feeling of hubris.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T18:27:00-08:00","id":354225,"title":"","content":"Those are only sample questions. You are allowed to narrow down the possible answers to only people present, but that does not mean you -must- do so. Two very different things. Examples are only examples, we should look to the actual power description for its limitations.<br /> <br /> &quot;The vampire focuses on a single victim, peeling back the layers of lies and misdirection to reveal the truth underneath. The Beast sniffs out the victim\u2019s dark secrets, things that she doesn\u2019t want anyone else to know. What the vampire does with that information is up to him.&quot;<br /> &quot;This level of Auspex focuses on questions concerning the secrets and weaknesses of a single character.&quot;<br /> <br /> That's the only real guidance given. Who you hate most in the world can definitely be constituted both as a secret and an exploitable weakness; it checks out.<br /> <br /> Nobody is saying that Auspex 1 lets you know things about people not present, that's true. Not even sure why you brought that up. They're different powers in their entirety. Notice how Auspex 1 specifically points out that only immediate stuff can be perceived, while Auspex 2 <b>does not</b>. Your assertion that Uncanny Perception is only about things that are immediately relevant seems a bit shaky when they found the space to specifically mention that in one power, but not this one. Also notice how Beast's Hackles says that &quot;the sample questions below cover much of the information the Beast can provide.&quot;, while Uncanny Perception doesn't (again). Why? Becauce Uncanny Perception is much less limited, and the examples there are a far smaller grasp of what is possible than is the case for Beast's Hackles, and its examples are thus not representative of the full scope of the ability. Trying to determine the scope of Auspex 2 based upon Auspex 1 is quite meaningless.<br /> <br /> On the topic of the descriptions: &quot;[Auspex shows the user] visions that range from the direct to the hallucinatory.&quot; I would consider all the visions in the example to be of the direct variety. They are immediately overlaid onto reality; however, when somebody isn't present I could easily see an image representing them in a metaphorical way appearing in the Mekhet's mind's eye. It is no surprise that they represented it so one-sidedly, since direct visions tend to require less context to get it, while more metaphorical ones would possibly confuse players outside of a context they had no room to create.<br /> <br /> It is of no surprise that the current Auspex is seen as not much improved or even inferior to the last one when people choose to add limitations to the text that were never written there based only upon a non-inclusive list of examples.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":1292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","user":"Unahim","date":". 12-29-2014, 09:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T19:25:14-08:00","id":354317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=354225#post354225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobody is saying that Auspex 1 lets you know things about people not present, that's true. Not even sure why you brought that up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was saying that the example question of Uncanny Perception clearly only talks about people who are present, and I was supporting my point by saying the wording is similar to the wording of Beast's Hackles. I hope you'll pardon my lack of trust, but this is the internet. It seems obvious, but I wouldn't have been particularly surprised if someone had tried to argue the point, so I put in some arguments preemptively. But it was obviously not needed and everyone can move on.<br /> <br /> I pretty much take exactly the opposite approach. The text is <i>incredibly vague</i>. How am I supposed to find limitations in a sentence like &quot;The Beast sniffs out the victim\u2019s dark secrets, things that she doesn\u2019t want anyone else to know.&quot; or &quot;This level of Auspex focuses on questions concerning the secrets and weaknesses of a single character.&quot; ? It literally just says &quot;this power lets you find secrets&quot;. That's not a limitation. That's just... anything. Everything. And since there is no limitation in the text, you have to check the example questions. And all the examples given follow my understanding: they're either very important facets of the target's personality (like psychological problems or Vice), or they are things that concern the current situation. That doesn't look like chance, like it just so happened that, randomly, the examples ended up all being like that but actually you can do anything you want. That looks like that's how they think Auspex 2 should work.<br /> <br /> I mean, do you sincerely think a Mekhet can look at someone and ask: &quot;does this person want to betray the Prince?&quot; &quot;are they planning something?&quot; &quot;are they planning to kill the Prince?&quot; &quot;are they going to do it in the next year?&quot; &quot;are they going to do it in the next month?&quot; and so on and so forth, spending time and Vitae until they know everything, every &quot;secret&quot; there is to know? If so, then why haven't you houseruled it? How does that make for an enjoyable game? How is that supposed to work when everything is supposed to be about politics and backstabbing and scheming? (And suddenly Elderand's comments about how the Mekhet clan should be ostracized make perfect sense...)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=354225#post354225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is of no surprise that the current Auspex is seen as not much improved or even inferior to the last one when people choose to add limitations to the text that were never written there based only upon a non-inclusive list of examples.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would have said it's no surprise people think 2e Auspex is vastly improved if they've decided it lets you find out literally <i>anything</i> about someone, with zero limitations, without any way of resisting or contesting. Why would you even waste your time learning Auspex 4 if Auspex 2 can already do everything? It doesn't even let you work particularly faster, as Elderand implied earlier in the thread (I think he called it the &quot;brute force way&quot;?). You could actually say it's a inferior, since it's 1 Vitae = 1 memory, instead of 1 Vitae = a bunch of questions, and it's also contested. An interpretation of Auspex 2 that makes half of Auspex 4 almost pointless is not, I think, likely to be what the writers intended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":815,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","user":"Kazorh","date":". 12-29-2014, 10:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T22:25:09-08:00","id":354475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=348130#post348130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You suffer Breaking Points for doing inhuman things like surviving something that would kill a mortal</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This sounds like a very poor mechanic in world where Vampires have to contend with Hunters, Werewolves, and who knows what else trying to kill them on sight! Like Jack said <b>&quot;Self preservation is a vital part of humanity!&quot;</b><br /> <br /> <br /> Humans don't suffer moral degredation from surviving near death experiences...<br /> <br /> <br /> -------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>List of triggers for this:</b><br /> <br /> Multiple stab wounds<br /> <br /> Gunshot wounds to the torso / head<br /> <br /> Many offensive supernatural powers<br /> <br /> Hit by a vehicle<br /> <br /> Collapsed under a building<br /> <br /> Have your face clawed off.<br /> <br /> Have your limbs cut off.<br /> <br /> Broken Neck<br /> <br /> Ran out of ideas.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 12-30-2014, 01:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-29T23:13:24-08:00","id":354511,"title":"","content":"Humanity is not about moral degradation in second edition, so that's okay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T01:15:44-08:00","id":354556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=354475#post354475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This sounds like a very poor mechanic in world where Vampires have to contend with Hunters, Werewolves, and who knows what else trying to kill them on sight! Like Jack said <b>&quot;Self preservation is a vital part of humanity!&quot;</b></div> </div> </div> </div>You don't lose Humanity for defending yourself. You lose it when you experience something that reminds you that you're not human. Humanity breaking points are also still scaled like 1e (though a very different scale), so dropping below Humanity 7 means surviving what would put a human in the hospital stops bothering you (unlike Integrity where breaking points don't go away with lower Integrity).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Humans don't suffer moral degredation from surviving near death experiences... </div> </div> </div>2e has moved away from these traits representing moral degradation.<br /> <br /> Integrity is about how well you keep your sense of self in the face of emotional/mental traumas. You can most certainly end up losing Integrity from surviving a near death experience; especially if from a supernatural source.<br /> <br /> Humanity is about how well your vampire maintains their ability to connect to being human. That's why things that remind you of your inhumanity are breaking points. Lasting 100 years as a vampire, or gaining BP 6 are both breaking points (and worse ones than getting beat to shit and walking away). There's no inherent moral difference between Humanity 10 and Humanity 1. Though low Humanity vampires would appear less moral than high Humanity vampires, because their morality would not communicate as one that humans would understand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T01:52:57-08:00","id":354581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=354511#post354511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Humanity is not about moral degradation in second edition, so that's okay.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was making a comparison, actually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T02:25:49-08:00","id":354623,"title":"","content":"A comparison to what?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T05:17:04-08:00","id":354679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=354556#post354556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though low Humanity vampires would appear less moral than high Humanity vampires, because their morality would not communicate as one that humans would understand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Similarly you could have a vampire lose certain immoral features as their humanity lowered. Perhaps a medieval torturer loses the love for his &quot;art&quot;, as he becomes more animal like over the centuries, he feels less of a compulsion to inflict harm, the psychological drive to do it being very human.<br /> <br /> I've always imagined low humanity vampires to be like sentient vipers, rather than monsters, i.e. amoral vs immoral.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T06:53:24-08:00","id":354703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=354475#post354475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This sounds like a very poor mechanic in world where Vampires have to contend with Hunters, Werewolves, and who knows what else trying to kill them on sight! Like Jack said <b>&quot;Self preservation is a vital part of humanity!&quot;</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's a mechanic in Vampire: the Requiem Second Edition. You can use it or you can houserule it out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=354475#post354475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Humans don't suffer moral degredation from surviving near death experiences...</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither do vampires. They suffer Humanity detachment, which as I said in the quote you posted, no longer represents how well the character keeps to a moral code, but has changed to reflect how in touch they are with the human experience.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=354475#post354475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>List of triggers for this:</b><br /> <br /> Multiple stab wounds<br /> <br /> Gunshot wounds to the torso / head<br /> <br /> Many offensive supernatural powers<br /> <br /> Hit by a vehicle<br /> <br /> Collapsed under a building<br /> <br /> Have your face clawed off.<br /> <br /> Have your limbs cut off.<br /> <br /> Broken Neck<br /> <br /> Ran out of ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, all of these things would, in fact, trigger a Breaking Point roll for a vampire of Humanity 8 or higher.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T07:10:18-08:00","id":354709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=354475#post354475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This sounds like a very poor mechanic in world where Vampires have to contend with Hunters, Werewolves, and who knows what else trying to kill them on sight! Like Jack said <b>&quot;Self preservation is a vital part of humanity!&quot;</b></div> </div> </div> </div>It's a trying challenge to maintain a high level of Humanity, that mental and emotional link to the living being you once were, if you're living the natural unlife of a vampire. It is, however, pretty manageable to level out comfortably at a medium or lower level of Humanity while doing all the things that are thematically common and expected of vampire PCs who might have to get into shootouts or deal with rabid werewolves.<br /> <br /> Humanity isn't meant as a punishment mechanic. There's some intended tension of give-and-take, but losing Humanity is not supposed to be something that results if you make the wrong choice or do things you shouldn't. You're supposed to end up in stressful, taxing situations, and just as you might limp out of them with physical wounds, you might stagger out of them with spiritual or emotional wounds. Unlike your physical health, though, your psyche can callous, becoming inured with experience towards certain levels of stress; that's settling at a lower Humanity rating. But that's moving away from the human baseline. Humans don't weather catastrophic damage calmly and unbothered. You let yourself become a little more of a monster in order to endure and thrive.<br /> <br /> A beast I am, lest a beast I become.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T15:34:41-08:00","id":355180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=354317#post354317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-snip-</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much all of the worry about a Mekhet finding out everything about everyone is solved by the fact that the visions are cryptic in nature. The more complex the thing you're trying to find out, the harder it'll be. Every time I've used Auspex I've had to use other methods to confirm the suspicion, and you know what? Sometimes I couldn't confirm it, because my assumption based upon a metaphorical hallucination was wrong. What exactly do you think &quot;Does this person want to betray the Prince?&quot; is going to look like in a cryptic vision? What are you going to do once you get your &quot;information&quot;? Kill them because you saw a vision where two shadows danced around each other with knives? Clearly they want to kill the Prince! Why would anyone believe you saw what you saw, though? Maybe you're just trying to get power yourself. Then you make the big reveal, and everyone laughs: Turns out they're the best of friends and knife duels, their favourite passtime training activity together, embodies that friendship. Well isn't your face red! (Just a tongue-in-cheek example, don't get too hung up on it. Point is auspex 2 doesn't make you sure of your case, and provides no evidence for anyone else to see.)<br /> <br /> Auspex 4 has plenty of value because it's super clear, no mistakes possible in interpretation. It still has a wider scope than Auspex 2, too. If you're trying to infiltrate a place and some guy asks you &quot;Password?&quot; picking the password from his mind will work, asking with Auspex 2 will not. Similarly, the full contents of somebody's conversation with another person last night will be impossible for auspex 2, but not for auspex 4. On top of that, you can inflict conditions on people. I really feel it's not fair to pretend a wider scope of questions for auspex 2 invalidates auspex 4 when it is so obviously not the case. I'm very excited to be picking up Auspex 4 on my character in just a few more experience points.<br /> <br /> So we haven't found any actual rules supporting the limitations you think are there, and I really do think your reasoning for why the limitation -should- be there is rather moot, since as I've just said a capable ST already gets all the tools to limit the power (and make it really fun and engaging to use to boot) right in the description of the power itself. You are of course free to impose a house rule limiting the scope of the power, but without any actual rules support I do have to mark it as such.<br /> <br /> Also, don't imply that I said that &quot;randomly&quot; by &quot;chance&quot; all examples ended up being one way. I give a very specific reason why they could be that way, which is not dependant on chance or randomness at all, but ease of writing and word count. It irks me a bit that you dismiss such an argument as being the same as random chance.<br /> <br /> TL;DR: You grossly dramatize the power of Auspex 2 when not employing your proposed houserule, marginalize all of several advantages of auspex 4 compared to it (or just forget them entirely), and misrepresent my arguments dealing with why the examples, which still have no powers of limitation, are the way they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":1292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","user":"Unahim","date":". 12-30-2014, 06:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T15:45:19-08:00","id":355188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=354709#post354709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a trying challenge to maintain a high level of Humanity, that mental and emotional link to the living being you once were, if you're living the natural unlife of a vampire. It is, however, pretty manageable to level out comfortably at a medium or lower level of Humanity while doing all the things that are thematically common and expected of vampire PCs who might have to get into shootouts or deal with rabid werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ironic that nWoD have Kindred much more likely have to deal with hostile Sin-Eaters, Changelings, and Prometheans than the Uratha.<br /> <br /> Sin-Eaters because you're 28th victim simply won't stay dead and they aren't a Reverent. Changelings because you're too much like the True Fae for them to handle, and Prometheans because nothing frustrates a Prince more than Wasteland creeping into his/her city.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T03:22:41-08:00","id":355573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=355180#post355180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty much all of the worry about a Mekhet finding out everything about everyone is solved by the fact that the visions are cryptic in nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another irreconcilable difference in our interpretations, I suppose. The visions are cryptic because that makes it cooler and more flavorful, not because the player shouldn't be able to tell what the answer actually is. That's why it says the answer should <i>include</i> &quot;the imagery conjured by the Beast&quot;, not that it <i>should only be</i> imagery. You give misleading information (like the knife fighting of friendship) for dramatic failures, not because you felt like messing with your players.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=355180#post355180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What exactly do you think &quot;Does this person want to betray the Prince?&quot; is going to look like in a cryptic vision?</div> </div> </div> </div>A sinister smile for yes? A vision of the target kneeling in submission for no? A dagger in their hand for yes? A feeling of fear and a whimper for no? Should I go on?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=355180#post355180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're trying to infiltrate a place and some guy asks you &quot;Password?&quot; picking the password from his mind will work, asking with Auspex 2 will not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not? It's a secret. Use Uncanny Perception, ask &quot;what's the password?&quot; and the ST gets to choose between a creepy voice whispering the answer in your ear or bloody letters spelling it out on the wall or whatever else they can imagine.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=355180#post355180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">as I've just said a capable ST already gets all the tools to limit the power</div> </div> </div> </div>Apart from misleading information (which, as I said, should be limited to dramatic failures), you've talked about questions you feel couldn't be answered by Auspex 2, but I don't understand what your criteria actually are. Care to enlighten me?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=355180#post355180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would anyone believe you saw what you saw, though?</div> </div> </div> </div>So what? You can help them or sabotage them or play 20 questions until you find out about some sort of proof. Or just bash their head in because you're the Sheriff and you don't answer to anyone except the Prince. Or develop a reputation for being always right, until you saying something like that publicly will instill enough doubt in everyone's mind that you've still hurt them politically. Or use any other of the infinite possibilities created by the fact that you know everything about everyone's schemes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=355180#post355180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On top of that, you can inflict conditions on people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why, yes. I did say it made <b>half</b> of Auspex 4 <b>almost</b> pointless. Remember: from my point of view, Auspex 2 has some important limitations, and the memory viewing part of Auspex 4 is the moment you do away with those limitations. Compared to that, Conditions are less impressive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=355180#post355180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I give a very specific reason why they could be that way, which is not dependant on chance or randomness at all, but ease of writing and word count.</div> </div> </div> </div>You... didn't? You said &quot;the examples there are a far smaller grasp of what is possible than is the case for Beast's Hackles&quot; and &quot;its examples are thus not representative of the full scope of the ability&quot;, but unless I've recently become blind, you didn't talk about <i>why</i>. Also, really? Ease of writing? Word count? They could have removed either the &quot;right now&quot; in the question about fear or the &quot;here&quot; in the question about hate. That way, there would have been one question concerned with who is immediately present, and one question with no such limit. There, done. People like me wouldn't be under the impression that this is meant to be a limitation on the whole dot of Auspex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":815,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","user":"Kazorh","date":". 12-31-2014, 06:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T10:16:29-08:00","id":356687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=350824#post350824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">old Auspex 4 was even more powerful then the current version is.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I disagree with this, if only because auspex 4 now lets you give the victim traumatizing memories now that can inflict conditions instead of just mind reading and general telepathy (Which it still does). Imagine being subjected to all the emotions felt during a violent embrace, or a bout of frenzy resulting in a friends death or something? Scary stuff can be done with Auspex 4 beyond just gaining deeper secrets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":460,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","user":"Rani Neferet","date":". 01-01-2015, 01:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T10:46:06-08:00","id":356693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=356687#post356687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I disagree with this, if only because auspex 4 now lets you give the victim traumatizing memories now that can inflict conditions instead of just mind reading and general telepathy (Which it still does). Imagine being subjected to all the emotions felt during a violent embrace, or a bout of frenzy resulting in a friends death or something? Scary stuff can be done with Auspex 4 beyond just gaining deeper secrets.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was already able to do that with Auspex 4 in the VtR version. It was cost free to use on humans. I could also carry on an entire conversation with someone in a room full of people who couldn't hear anything we were saying. You can't do that anymore because you'll run out of vitae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T19:52:36-08:00","id":357157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Audrey St. John</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=356693#post356693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't do that anymore because you'll run out of vitae.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not true. You only need to spend additional Vitae to drag up memories of the past. You can still read and project for the whole scene with only the basic cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":815,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","user":"Kazorh","date":". 01-01-2015, 11:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T00:33:02-08:00","id":357313,"title":"","content":"You can read one person's thoughts for an entire scene, drag up a memory or insert one of your own at any point during the scene.<br /> You're forgetting, the target does not automatically get access to your thoughts, memories or mood, you have to insert those yourself. (Otherwise everyone's a telepath. That may make for some interesting repercussions but in general, I don't assume that.) Subsequent insertions cost Vitae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":190,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","user":"Audrey St. John","date":". 01-02-2015, 03:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T03:03:17-08:00","id":357367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=356687#post356687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I disagree with this, if only because auspex 4 now lets you give the victim traumatizing memories now that can inflict conditions instead of just mind reading and general telepathy (Which it still does). Imagine being subjected to all the emotions felt during a violent embrace, or a bout of frenzy resulting in a friends death or something? Scary stuff can be done with Auspex 4 beyond just gaining deeper secrets.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah, you're right. At the time I was mostly concerning myself with my mind reading. With this, Auspex 4 is more powerful.<br /> <br /> And to Kazorth, having the password magic up, would be beyond what Auspex 2 is capable of in my head. It works with what can be seen on the person - password to a computer is not something seen on a person, nor is it about a single person (the power does say that it concerns itself with secrets and weaknesses of a single character). Also looking up the examples, password's and anything in such detail is beyond it. The additional questions, imo, should be as specific (or non specific) as the example one's...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T04:44:52-08:00","id":357394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Audrey St. John</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=357313#post357313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can read one person's thoughts for an entire scene, drag up a memory or insert one of your own at any point during the scene.<br /> You're forgetting, the target does not automatically get access to your thoughts, memories or mood, you have to insert those yourself. (Otherwise everyone's a telepath. That may make for some interesting repercussions but in general, I don't assume that.) Subsequent insertions cost Vitae.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I see it, the first paragraph of the power is what you can do with only the basic cost. The sentence &quot;He can also project thoughts, either speaking directly into the victim's thoughts or depositing a mental image or memory.&quot; is in the first paragraph. The second paragraph concerns itself with dragging up past memories, and is the one with the sentence &quot;Uncovering further memories costs 1 Vitae per memory.&quot; Nowhere does it say you need to spend additional Vitae to project.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=357367#post357367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And to Kazorth, having the password magic up, would be beyond what Auspex 2 is capable of in my head. It works with what can be seen on the person - password to a computer is not something seen on a person, nor is it about a single person (the power does say that it concerns itself with secrets and weaknesses of a single character). Also looking up the examples, password's and anything in such detail is beyond it. The additional questions, imo, should be as specific (or non specific) as the example one's...</div> </div> </div> </div>So does it work if the person is the only one who knows the password, which makes it the secret of a single character?<br /> <br /> For the record, I don't think Auspex 2 should ever be able to find out a password: my point was that I have no idea why Unahim thinks the same thing, and I wanted to know his thought process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T05:43:14-08:00","id":357426,"title":"","content":"It's technically fair game for Auspex 2. It is a secret and it is something the target doesn't want anyone else to know, especially if it's the password to their computer or home security system. The vision could show hands typing in the code or the smell of dead fish (password is mackerel). Committing diablerie ten years ago can't be seen on a person either, but technically it's detectable. Personally I wouldn't allow password stealing or much of the other crap trotted out as obtainable via Auspex 2 use alone, simply because things like computer passwords and individual aspirations involves concepts above and beyond the Beast's cognitive ability to discern much less describe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-02T08:39:51-08:00","id":357497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=357394#post357394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So does it work if the person is the only one who knows the password, which makes it the secret of a single character?<br /> <br /> For the record, I don't think Auspex 2 should ever be able to find out a password: my point was that I have no idea why Unahim thinks the same thing, and I wanted to know his thought process.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, it was just an example, and since you agree with it - there's nothing to discuss here.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T07:08:53-08:00","id":359096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rani Neferet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=356687#post356687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I disagree with this, if only because auspex 4 now lets you give the victim traumatizing memories now that can inflict conditions instead of just mind reading and general telepathy (Which it still does). Imagine being subjected to all the emotions felt during a violent embrace, or a bout of frenzy resulting in a friends death or something? Scary stuff can be done with Auspex 4 beyond just gaining deeper secrets.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And rereading Auspex 4 reveals that this is false. You cannot give the victim traumatizing memories and inflict conditions. What the power does, is allows the surfacing of the users memories and inflicting memories related to them. <br /> <br /> Book says: &quot; By focusing, the vampire can drag up a full memory from the<br /> victim, including things that the victim has forgotten or that<br /> were suppressed by magic (though doing so takes a Clash of<br /> Wills). He experiences all of the memory in an instant, with all<br /> five senses. If he chooses to transmit that memory to the victim,<br /> he can inflict a Condition like Guilty, Inspired, or Shaken as<br /> appropriate (p. 302 and p. 305). Uncovering further memories<br /> costs 1 Vitae per memory.&quot;<br /> <br /> drag up a memory from the victim, if he chooses to transmit THAT memory to the victim...<br /> <br /> this basically tells me that you're resurfacing memories (either forgotten, hidden, or otherwise) to the front of his mind thus inflicting related conditions. For example he cheated on his wife? Bring that memory back so he feels guilty about it. He was terrified by Nosferatu Y? Bring that memory back, so he's scared again. Ventrue Z dominated him into murdering his sister and made him forget it? Bring that back for some juicy conditions.<br /> <br /> ou got a young protected kid who doesn't have any guilty/terrific memories in his head? This part of power is basically useless on him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T07:17:40-08:00","id":359102,"title":"","content":"For some reason it doesn't allow me to edit my previous post, so I'm sorry for a double... triple post. <br /> Anyways, I found this, when a player in a different game used the power to make someone terrified of me &quot;By conjuring up memories of disgust and fear&quot; bla bla bla. The whole thing... felt like nightmare to me, and thinking more, if such freedom is allowed with Auspex 4, one can easily duplicate low levels of Nightmare and Majesty with it by bringing up good and bad memories. That feels very wrong to me, since that's not Auspex. That's Nightmare and Majesty. <br /> <br /> Auspex is for bringing up the truths and memories and bringing them to the front of the world. Not for creating false images of the world by conjuring things which ain't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T08:51:25-08:00","id":359174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=359096#post359096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And rereading Auspex 4 reveals that this is false. You cannot give the victim traumatizing memories and inflict conditions. What the power does, is allows the surfacing of the users memories and inflicting memories related to them.<br /> <br /> Book says: &quot; By focusing, the vampire can drag up a full memory from the<br /> victim, including things that the victim has forgotten or that<br /> were suppressed by magic (though doing so takes a Clash of<br /> Wills). He experiences all of the memory in an instant, with all<br /> five senses. If he chooses to transmit that memory to the victim,<br /> he can inflict a Condition like Guilty, Inspired, or Shaken as<br /> appropriate (p. 302 and p. 305). Uncovering further memories<br /> costs 1 Vitae per memory.&quot;<br /> <br /> drag up a memory from the victim, if he chooses to transmit THAT memory to the victim...<br /> <br /> this basically tells me that you're resurfacing memories (either forgotten, hidden, or otherwise) to the front of his mind thus inflicting related conditions. For example he cheated on his wife? Bring that memory back so he feels guilty about it. He was terrified by Nosferatu Y? Bring that memory back, so he's scared again. Ventrue Z dominated him into murdering his sister and made him forget it? Bring that back for some juicy conditions.<br /> <br /> ou got a young protected kid who doesn't have any guilty/terrific memories in his head? This part of power is basically useless on him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your quote seems to be unfinished. Is that how it looks in the book? If so, there is some contradictory (or at least very confusing) information there.<br /> <br /> You can dredge up memories in the Victim (You do not need to transmit them to the Victim, since they are already his memories).<br /> You can transmit Memories to the Victim - Seems like that is implying that you can take someone else's memories (you know, Like your Own) and inflict them upon your victim. As a result, they pick up some potential conditions.<br /> <br /> To me, it seems like you can do both, yes?<br /> <br /> As to your allusion to Nightmare and Majesty, You are not really duplicating their effects, are you? Are the Effects and Conditions that you inflict the same ones that Nightmare and Majesty Inflict?<br /> If so, then I can see where you have that opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T10:30:34-08:00","id":359290,"title":"","content":"It's a direct quote, and it's a single paragraph from the book. That gives me the information, which tells me, that Information can be pulled and THAT information, can be used to inflict conditions. <br /> By resurfacing long forgotten memories, hidden memories or stuff we'd rather forget. <br /> As for Nightmare and Majesty. Yes, you are duplicating the effects. For example, if you bring back the memories of me scaring the shit out of someone, what's the most appropriate condition on the target? Frigtened, Scared or some other on this.. which is pretty much duplication <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> To repeat, let's see what the quote says You can draw memories, which you feel with all 5 of your senses. If you choose to transmit that memory to the victim you get to inflict a condition. This is a little bit para phrasing, but it looks pretty clear to me. (besides the fact, that it's really easy to miss)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T12:12:54-08:00","id":359370,"title":"","content":"The first paragraph has a blanket statement that you can project memories, so yes, you could project your own memories to someone. But from the way the second paragraph is phrased (and I am agreeing with Griautis' reading 100% here), I've always assumed that only their own memories could inflict Conditions on a victim. Like, those are the only ones that are personal enough for it.<br /> <br /> Or else you kind of get the question of why aren't you inflicting Conditions on <i>yourself</i> every time you read a scary memory? After all, you experience it when you read it, and if experiencing that memory inflicts a Condition on every one <i>else</i>...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T12:45:59-08:00","id":359434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=359370#post359370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first paragraph has a blanket statement that you can project memories, so yes, you could project your own memories to someone. But from the way the second paragraph is phrased (and I am agreeing with Griautis' reading 100% here), I've always assumed that only their own memories could inflict Conditions on a victim. Like, those are the only ones that are personal enough for it.<br /> <br /> Or else you kind of get the question of why aren't you inflicting Conditions on <i>yourself</i> every time you read a scary memory? After all, you experience it when you read it, and if experiencing that memory inflicts a Condition on every one <i>else</i>...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you only have their memories and your own to work with, you can't just make up memories that neither of you actually have. That's Dominate's wheelhouse. And given how jaded vampires tend to be, theyre not likely to be empathetic enough for someone else's traumatic memory to bother them. I might allow that to work on mortals - some poor sap having the memory of a violent embrace being forced into his mind? I might even call that an Integrity Breaking Point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T14:55:01-08:00","id":359574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=359370#post359370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or else you kind of get the question of why aren't you inflicting Conditions on <i>yourself</i> every time you read a scary memory? After all, you experience it when you read it, and if experiencing that memory inflicts a Condition on every one <i>else</i>...</div> </div> </div> </div>Because then they would just farm positive Conditions for the benefits and the minor negative ones for xp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-04T22:57:19-08:00","id":359910,"title":"","content":"Now I'm imagining a crazy Mekhet who seeks out people who've lived through traumatic events to add to his collection of bad memories. A connoisseur of pain, if you will.<br /> <br /> Then he gets all excited about sharing it with you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T01:34:48-08:00","id":360013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=359910#post359910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I'm imagining a crazy Mekhet who seeks out people who've lived through traumatic events to add to his collection of bad memories. A connoisseur of pain, if you will.<br /> <br /> Then he gets all excited about sharing it with you.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And that feels like Nightmare story wise. Really, such usage of Auspex steps on SO many toes of other disciplines that it hurts me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T04:35:58-08:00","id":360108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=360013#post360013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And that feels like Nightmare story wise. Really, such usage of Auspex steps on SO many toes of other disciplines that it hurts me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you be opposed to Green Eyes (Majesty 3) being used to induce fear of loss? Or the Lying Mind (Dominate 4) to create a horrifying memory?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T05:02:06-08:00","id":360122,"title":"","content":"No, but those are examples on a totally different level. Sadly, Auspex 4, if allowed to do so, can directly duplicate the effects of Nightmare 2 and Majesty 2. <br /> And tell me, what's the difference between Auspex 4, pushing in memories of fear and making you run from me and with Nightmare 2? how exactly nightmare 2 works? By creating what's not real.<br /> The problem I have with such usage, is that thematically such usage does not fit Auspex whatsoever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T06:41:01-08:00","id":360174,"title":"","content":"&quot;Auspex turns the Beast's predatory instincts loose on secrets, finding points of weakness and hidden gems for the vampire to exploit to his advantage.&quot;<br /> <br /> That is the very first sentence in the BS book describing Auspex in the Disciplines chapter. So exactly how is pulling out memories of fear and using them against your character NOT thematic usage of Auspex when fear is a fundamental exploitable weakness of everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T06:58:50-08:00","id":360184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Audrey St. John</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=360174#post360174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Auspex turns the Beast's predatory instincts loose on secrets, finding points of weakness and hidden gems for the vampire to exploit to his advantage.&quot;<br /> <br /> That is the very first sentence in the BS book describing Auspex in the Disciplines chapter. So exactly how is pulling out memories of fear and using them against your character NOT thematic usage of Auspex when fear is a fundamental exploitable weakness of everyone.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> finding hidden weaknesses and hidden gems is all great and awesome. Do it. Find out what I'm afraid. pull it back. It's all very thematic for Auspex.<br /> <br /> However, pushing your own memories of fear upon me? That smells of Nightmare. Pushing good memories/feelings? Smells of Majesty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T07:55:11-08:00","id":360205,"title":"","content":"But Nightmare and Majesty users get that ability 2 dots sooner... I honestly do not have much of a problem with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T07:59:05-08:00","id":360208,"title":"","content":"As I said, my biggest problem is thematic here. Such usage of Auspex definitely falls off the &quot;Find out and abuse secrets&quot; into the realm of &quot;make him afraid/happy out of nothing&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T10:56:50-08:00","id":360298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=360122#post360122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, but those are examples on a totally different level. Sadly, Auspex 4, if allowed to do so, can directly duplicate the effects of Nightmare 2 and Majesty 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. Dread Presence and Confidant create very specific and very complex emotional states with a variety of effects. A charmed victim implicitly trusts her charmer and wants to do favors for him. A Frightened victim feels in mortal danger from the vampire and wants to get away from him at all costs. Someone whose bad memories have been brought to the surface feel bad about the time that thing happened. To me, the biggest difference is that Majesty and Nightmare affect how the victim feels about the user. Auspex 4 can only show the victim a scary or nice thing, it can't actually control how they react to it and it can't force an association between that image and the vampire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=360122#post360122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And tell me, what's the difference between Auspex 4, pushing in memories of fear and making you run from me and with Nightmare 2? how exactly nightmare 2 works? By creating what's not real.</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference is, the former might leave the victim Shaken or Spooked, depending on how they feel about the memory - they remembered or were shown something horrifying and it may rattle them a bit, if it happens to be a vision of something that disturbs them. The later will directly alter the victim's emotional state and forcibly change it to a flight response, with the vampire as the source of danger.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=360122#post360122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem I have with such usage, is that thematically such usage does not fit Auspex whatsoever.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. I think you are focusing too much on the results and not enough on the methods. In my opinion, using someone's horrible secret thoughts and memories directly as a weapon is much more thematically appropriate than what amounts to astral projection is, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T12:17:22-08:00","id":360408,"title":"","content":"We're a lot closer in our opinions than it might look. The way you use it and describe it - fits completely under my views <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T13:26:57-08:00","id":360521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=360298#post360298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree. I think you are focusing too much on the results and not enough on the methods. In my opinion, using someone's horrible secret thoughts and memories directly as a weapon is much more thematically appropriate than what amounts to astral projection is, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>You make a good point about Auspex. For what it's worth with regards to Astral Projection, I think part of the idea there is being the ultimate hidden observer, particularly since you're able to use other Auspex abilities while projected. The Beast, using its ability to reach out into the essence of others (telepathy, sensing secrets, etc.) extrudes your own essence to allow you to traverse the world as a projection, out of your body.<br /> <br /> That's how I've tried to reconcile it anyway. I think all the powers are in the same conceptual neighborhood, Auspex just seems less obviously connected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T14:10:10-08:00","id":360588,"title":"","content":"I agree, I actually think Auspex 5 fits in fine thematically. It's not quite as natural an extension of the concept as the other levels, but it doesn't really bother me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T14:55:53-08:00","id":360634,"title":"","content":"Auspex is about perception. At Auspex 5 you can become pure Perception, free from the bondage of the physical body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T13:33:11-08:00","id":363758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=348785#post348785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ventrue were prone to insanity, now they just have slightly more trouble with touchstones (it seems to be the conscencus that their clan weakness is a joke)</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, looking at it from an abstract mechanical point of view, I can see how it looks like the &quot;nicest&quot; bane to have, but in actual play I have found it as punishing as the others. When a Ventrue begins to lose humanity they really plummet down the ladder, possibly reaching Humanity 3 quite fast, only stabilising there because the acts you have to commit to go further are willfully inhuman, rather than something you might typically encounter as a vampire.<br /> <br /> Of course one can &quot;buy&quot; an extra touchstone with the merit, but as with all merits this has to be justified in the narrative and it's reasonably difficult for you to really develop a relationship with somebody that makes you reconnect to your humanity.<br /> <br /> If I'm a Ventrue, let's say my touchstone was my nephew who was only eight or nine when I was sired. I see him grow up, watch over him as he goes to college, has a family of his own. Then me and my Daeva associate have to break somebody's mind for information. We're both changed by the experience, more animalistic, amoral. However the Daeva still goes to see her sister at the weekends. However after breaking that guys mind, I literally don't give two fucks about my nephew any more (mechanically: touchstone detached). That is going to be very hard to recover, to either rebuild that connection or forge another as meaningful. In the mean time I have become much more prone to losing my human nature and if I do, I'm going to have to work even harder to regain what I lost. In the new edition the Ventrue are lords of emotional apathy and distance. I think it's a much more interesting weakness that the first edition's one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3326,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","user":"An Fhuiseog","date":". 01-08-2015, 04:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T23:22:45-08:00","id":364157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>An Fhuiseog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=363758#post363758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, looking at it from an abstract mechanical point of view, I can see how it looks like the &quot;nicest&quot; bane to have, but in actual play I have found it as punishing as the others. When a Ventrue begins to lose humanity they really plummet down the ladder, possibly reaching Humanity 3 quite fast, only stabilising there because the acts you have to commit to go further are willfully inhuman, rather than something you might typically encounter as a vampire.<br /> <br /> Of course one can &quot;buy&quot; an extra touchstone with the merit, but as with all merits this has to be justified in the narrative and it's reasonably difficult for you to really develop a relationship with somebody that makes you reconnect to your humanity.<br /> <br /> If I'm a Ventrue, let's say my touchstone was my nephew who was only eight or nine when I was sired. I see him grow up, watch over him as he goes to college, has a family of his own. Then me and my Daeva associate have to break somebody's mind for information. We're both changed by the experience, more animalistic, amoral. However the Daeva still goes to see her sister at the weekends. However after breaking that guys mind, I literally don't give two fucks about my nephew any more (mechanically: touchstone detached). That is going to be very hard to recover, to either rebuild that connection or forge another as meaningful. In the mean time I have become much more prone to losing my human nature and if I do, I'm going to have to work even harder to regain what I lost. In the new edition the Ventrue are lords of emotional apathy and distance. I think it's a much more interesting weakness that the first edition's one.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Semi false, as there's a difference between Having a Detached Touchstone and Losing a Touchstone. If you start to give no fucks and forget the exsistence of your nephew, you're gonna LOSE him, while now he's just DETACHED. <br /> <br /> The mechanical difference between the two is in the bonus to breaking point rolls. With all your Touchstones detached, you get a +0 bonus to your roll... However, if you lose all your touchstones it's a -2. So you still want to keep into contact with your nephew (so that you don't lose the touchstone at all), it just brings lesser benefits now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T11:34:56-08:00","id":364644,"title":"","content":"Depends how you interpret Detatched vs. Lost. In my games, you lose a Touchstone if they die or you burn bridges with them. I'f you're still in contact with them but the relationship doesn't hold the same meaning to you that it used to, they're detatched.<br /> <br /> I would consider my friend Alex a Detatched Touchstone - we haven't so much as talked to each other in years, we're both just different people than we were when we became friends and if I met him for the first time today, we would not become friends, we probably wouldn't even like each other. But even now, if he needed me for any reason at all, he would only have to ask and I would do it without a second thought and I know he would do the same for me. We're Detatched, but still each other's Touchstones. One of us would have to die, or to do something completely unforgivable to lose that connection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T11:50:30-08:00","id":364648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=364157#post364157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Semi false, as there's a difference between Having a Detached Touchstone and Losing a Touchstone. If you start to give no fucks and forget the exsistence of your nephew, you're gonna LOSE him, while now he's just DETACHED.<br /> <br /> The mechanical difference between the two is in the bonus to breaking point rolls. With all your Touchstones detached, you get a +0 bonus to your roll... However, if you lose all your touchstones it's a -2. So you still want to keep into contact with your nephew (so that you don't lose the touchstone at all), it just brings lesser benefits now.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're absolutely right Griautis, I guess &quot;suddenly care a good deal less&quot; would be better. I hope I'm right about new touchstone's being hard to form though, because it's what gave the Ventrue weakness its edge for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3326,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","user":"An Fhuiseog","date":". 01-09-2015, 06:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3326-an-fhuiseog","name":"An Fhuiseog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3326_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T12:11:07-08:00","id":364674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>An Fhuiseog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=364648#post364648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're absolutely right Griatis, I guess &amp;quot;suddenly care a good deal less&amp;quot; would be better. I hope I'm right about new touchstone's being hard to form though, because it's what gave the Ventrue weakness its edge for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that gaining a new Touchstone is not as easy as just spending an Experience point. You have to develop a very deep and meaningful relationship with the person (or place, or whatever). That takes a lot of time and effort, especially for a vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T14:48:08-08:00","id":364803,"title":"","content":"That said, there really should be no lack of things/people to choose as Touchstones, though.<br /> At least for a modern vampire, embraced fairly recently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T16:28:39-08:00","id":365850,"title":"","content":"It depends on your group how much you're going to want to roleplay it out, but no, bonding with a new Touchstone isn't easy. It's like finding a new friend you can tell anything -- hard to do on demand. And it's not like a vampire knows exactly what they're lacking, because a Touchstone is an abstraction of a set of Kindred psychological needs, not a supernatural slot in a vampire's soul.<br /> <br /> (EDIT: Although, obviously, a Touchstone isn't always a friend. Lots of relationships qualify, they just have to provide the appropriate psychological benefits in grounding the vampire.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 01-10-2015, 07:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T23:20:12-08:00","id":366091,"title":"","content":"I love the idea of a character whose touchstone is like their archnemisis so much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T23:33:07-08:00","id":366096,"title":"","content":"My touchstone is Gary Oak.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T06:05:45-08:00","id":366223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=366096#post366096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My touchstone is Gary Oak.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you were Ash the Vampire, that wouldn't be a stretch. Gary kept him focused on his goals!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-11T07:56:56-08:00","id":366282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=366096#post366096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My touchstone is Gary Oak.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mine is Sasuke Uchiha.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T13:40:07-08:00","id":829861,"title":"","content":"The Storytelling chapter changed a lot. Does anyone know why did they leave out the whole chronicle preparation stuff from Requiem 2nd edition? I love the TV series parallel and the listing of responsibilities in the Introduction, but Storytelling doesn't even have the &quot;Dos and don'ts&quot;. (At least Forsaken 2nd has those.) I think emphasizing cooperation among the players (and the ST) during building the player characters and the city; stressing the importance of a central theme and mood and keeping an eye on them was beautiful, the heart of what Vampire play meant for decades.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6216-p-czigany","name":"p.czigany","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T00:04:13-08:00","id":830069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>p.czigany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=829861#post829861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Storytelling chapter changed a lot. Does anyone know why did they leave out the whole chronicle preparation stuff from Requiem 2nd edition? I love the TV series parallel and the listing of responsibilities in the Introduction, but Storytelling doesn't even have the &quot;Dos and don'ts&quot;. (At least Forsaken 2nd has those.) I think emphasizing cooperation among the players (and the ST) during building the player characters and the city; stressing the importance of a central theme and mood and keeping an eye on them was beautiful, the heart of what Vampire play meant for decades.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know I wrote a pretty big chunk of that chapter. The reason I didn't bother with the 101 stuff was, at the time I wrote it, it wasn't going to be a core book. This was before we started doing Second Edition as a thing. This was even before we were adding core rules to the book. <br /> <br /> I was also the one who wrote the Dos and Donts in Forsaken 2e. By that point, things were a little different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T06:21:19-08:00","id":830980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=366091#post366091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love the idea of a character whose touchstone is like their archnemisis so much.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really want to play a Vampire whose Touchstone is a Hunter trying to kill him. I'd always fight him and play a stereotypical monster when in his presence. Always escape at the last moment, never hurt him too much. Such a good recipe for disaster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T06:53:38-08:00","id":830990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=830980#post830980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really want to play a Vampire whose Touchstone is a Hunter trying to kill him. I'd always fight him and play a stereotypical monster when in his presence. Always escape at the last moment, never hurt him too much. Such a good recipe for disaster.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A little theater to remind the vampire just what being a human (and a monster) is, even if they are the only one in on the joke?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T06:56:23-08:00","id":830992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=830990#post830990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> A little theater to remind the vampire just what being a human (and a monster) is, even if they are the only one in on the joke?</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. I think it'd work well... until the Hunter brings some friends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T07:11:23-08:00","id":830998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=830980#post830980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really want to play a Vampire whose Touchstone is a Hunter trying to kill him. I'd always fight him and play a stereotypical monster when in his presence. Always escape at the last moment, never hurt him too much. Such a good recipe for disaster.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure if you are into Anime, but I always argued that in Hellsing, Alexander Anderson (along with Integra and <i>possibly </i>the Police girl) was one of Alucard's Touchstones. The reaction at the end? A vampire losing one of their Touchstones. Even down to the whole part about encouraging Anderson to not forsake his own humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T07:11:50-08:00","id":830999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=830992#post830992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exactly. I think it'd work well... until the Hunter brings some friends.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> At which point the question must be asked: are they too protected by the rules of &quot;the game&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T07:53:19-08:00","id":831026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=830998#post830998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not sure if you are into Anime, but I always argued that in Hellsing, Alexander Anderson (along with Integra and <i>possibly </i>the Police girl) was one of Alucard's Touchstones. The reaction at the end? A vampire losing one of their Touchstones. Even down to the whole part about encouraging Anderson to not forsake his own humanity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like to understand what you said but I haven't watched Hellsing. All I know about it is that Alucard is a crazy weirdo vampire with guns who is really just Dracula gone gunslinger. Nothing wrong with that and probably a lot more character development in it, but that's what I know.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">At which point the question must be asked: are they too protected by the rules of &quot;the game&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>My guess would be no. It adds some tension and give the Hunter good reasons to keep hunting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T08:43:07-08:00","id":831049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=830999#post830999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At which point the question must be asked: are they too protected by the rules of &quot;the game&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Touchstones aren't really safe unless they get the True Friend merit, which probably wouldn't work for a vampire hunter.<br /> <br /> Vampire hunters and other enemies are fine touchstones. One of our players picked a hunter as one and they became sort of a twisted obsession for the vampire, who spied on them from afar and aclose, used their powers to subtly manipulate people around them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T09:39:18-08:00","id":831087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=831049#post831049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Touchstones aren't really safe unless they get the True Friend merit, which probably wouldn't work for a vampire hunter.<br /> <br /> Vampire hunters and other enemies are fine touchstones. One of our players picked a hunter as one and they became sort of a twisted obsession for the vampire, who spied on them from afar and aclose, used their powers to subtly manipulate people around them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant, does the vampire in question need to leave the &quot;other Heroes&quot; alive, or can they be killed since they are only &quot;supporting protagonists&quot; to the vampire's actual Touchstone.<br /> <br /> Or does introducing more characters into the farce of a morality play justify letting the vampire switch who the Touchstone is to one of the other Hunters (once appropriate interaction has happened, of course).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T09:55:27-08:00","id":831098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=831087#post831087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant, does the vampire in question need to leave the &quot;other Heroes&quot; alive, or can they be killed since they are only &quot;supporting protagonists&quot; to the vampire's actual Touchstone.</div> </div> </div> </div>A vampire can kill all of them, there's no rule against killing your touchstone, or the touchstone's buddies. Even if the vampire hunter was the subject of the True Friend merit, the player's vampire can kill them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or does introducing more characters into the farce of a morality play justify letting the vampire switch who the Touchstone is to one of the other Hunters (once appropriate interaction has happened, of course). </div> </div> </div>I think you could switch off to the 'lone survivor,' being your touchstone, as you say, provided there was appropriate interaction. I'd be surprised if it wasn't the case in at least one fictional example, with a vampire who finds a fondness more in the survival instinct of mortals, perhaps letting them get too close and always leaving the last one alive. But pulling it off would be exceedingly tricky, since there's no guarantee the last hunter would always build another cell around themselves. Still, it would be appropriate for a mastermind with a suicidal streak, who likes to play with fire because the chance of a final death makes them feel alive or something.<br /> <br /> Still, mechanically I think at that point your touchstone is not the specific lone survivor and, afterwards, the lone survivor of his cell. It would probably be with the concept of the hunter cell entirely. At least that's how I'd suggest it to a player who wanted to manage it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-16-2016, 01:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T11:06:03-08:00","id":831150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/348065-changes-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=831098#post831098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A vampire can kill all of them, there's no rule against killing your touchstone, or the touchstone's buddies. Even if the vampire hunter was the subject of the True Friend merit, the player's vampire can kill them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahhh. I think you are still misunderstanding my point. All the references to rules were merely regarding the theater of toying with the Hunter like a stereotypical villain. Of course they can kill whoever they want mechanically, but that will lose/detach the Touchstone (which is about portraying a villain in regards to this vampire hunter).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}